# Backend conventions

Full reference: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). Skill: [.cursor/skills/fastapi/SKILL.md](../skills/fastapi/SKILL.md).

## Layer responsibilities

| Layer | Path | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| Routers | `app/routers/` | Parse input, call service, return `ok()` — no business rules |
| Services | `app/services/` | Business logic and orchestration |
| Models | `app/models/` | SQLAlchemy schema only |
| Schemas | `app/schemas/` | Pydantic v2 request/response models |
| Shared | `app/shared/` | Reusable helpers (validation, enums, exceptions) |

## Patterns

- SQLAlchemy 2.0: `Mapped`, `mapped_column`, `select()`, `session.scalars()` — not `session.query()`
- Pydantic v2: `model_validate()`, `model_dump()`, `ConfigDict(from_attributes=True)`
- Domain errors: raise `AppError(code, _("message"), status_code=...)` with gettext strings
- API responses: use `ok(data)` from `app.schemas.responses`; follow [rest-api-standards.md](../../docs/rest-api-standards.md)
- UUID primary keys on new models
- Sync endpoints and DB access unless async is clearly justified

## Linting

Ruff (E, F, I) in `backend/pyproject.toml`. Run `make lint` / `make format` from repo root.

## Type checking

mypy runs incrementally on `app/services/` and `app/shared/` (`disallow_untyped_defs = true`). Run `make typecheck` or `mypy app/services app/shared` from `backend/`. Extend coverage to other packages later; do not block on 100% repo coverage.

## Do not

- Put business logic in routers
- Use `Base.metadata.create_all()` for schema changes
- Hand-write new Alembic migration files — change models, then user runs `make makemigrations MSG='...'`
